Original commit body from c36146a934d4fe656fda199e917881ec1b244f39:

htrac setup's sync-prerequisite check looked only for FORGEJO_TOKEN, while
htrac sync presents HG_GITHUB_TOKEN to a github origin. It warned on a
correctly configured github repository and passed one with only the
Codeberg token, which github.com rejects.

The token rule now lives in one table, sync.FORGE_TOKEN_VARS, with
forge_backend / forge_token / api_base_from_url helpers. Preflight, the
superseded-branch prune and setup check 22 all read it, with sync's own
.env parser and messages, and a parametrized test pins that the check and
sync agree for every backend/token pair.

Analogue fixed: prune_superseded_sync_branches took HG_GITHUB_TOKEN first
on every forge (sending the GitHub PAT to Codeberg when both were set) and
never looked at os.environ.

Also reported now: an origin URL that cannot be parsed; with no origin,
either token satisfies the token half.

